10
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
The Brood is a 1979 Canadian psychological body horror film written and directed by
David Cronenberg, and starring Oliver Reed, Samantha Eggar, and Art Hindle.

11
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:16,000
Its plot follows a man and his mentally ill ex-wife, who has been sequestered by
a psychiatrist known for his controversial therapy techniques.

12
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
A series of brutal unsolved murders serves as the
backdrop for the central narrative.

13
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:56,000
Written by Cronenberg after his own acrimonious divorce, he intended the screenplay as a meditation on a fractured relationship
between a husband and wife who share a child, and cast Eggar and Hindle as loose facsimiles of himself and his ex-wife.

14
00:53:40,000 --> 00:53:46,000
He would later state that, despite its incorporation of science fiction elements, he
considered it his sole feature that most embodied a "classic horror film".

15
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Principal photography of The Brood took place in late 1978
in Toronto on a budget of $1.5 million.

16
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
The film's score was composed by Howard Shore.

17
01:05:10,000 --> 01:05:16,000
Released in the spring of 1979 by New World Pictures, The Brood proved
profitable for the studio, grossing over $5 million.

18
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Though it initially received mixed reviews from critics, it would
establish itself as a cult film in the following decades.

19
01:12:50,000 --> 01:12:56,000
It has attracted scholarly interest from academics in the areas of film
theory for its themes regarding mental illness and parenthood.

20
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
In 2006, the Chicago Film Critics Association named it
the 88th scariest film of all time.

21
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
In 2013, it was selected for restoration by the Criterion
Collection, which subsequently released it on Blu-ray.

22
01:24:20,000 --> 01:24:26,000
The film explores themes of toronto, canada, mutant,
transformation, psychologist, divorce.

23
01:28:10,000 --> 01:28:16,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
